  $t$In run 42528 sol's cure lowered the challenger's count from 2 to 1, and the stored judgment (debate_judgments 1279) kept counted_premises_challenger [3,4] beside the count of 1. The cure did name the premise (enforcer row 54271, K-UNX "CHALLENGER premise 4", CURED, "CORRECTED COUNT 1 takes the premise out of the count"), but the engine carried cured items into the array only when they add a premise (pkgB6, R.cpAdd). Change, Shared Library only: the cure result also carries cpDrop, the premises CURED items took out of the count, and cureRewrite drops them from the array before pkgCPD, only when the drop equals the cut. Expected effect: the stored array agrees with the corrected count and an AUDIT v50 DERIVED line names the premise. Two things a judge can be sent change (plan rev 1): the judge enforcer prompt's STORED COUNTED PREMISES line, and a possible D38 BASIS gate item on a side the cure lowered. Not changed: reasoning, a model setting, a token limit, a prompt's instructions, a count. Part B (a premise list in the CORRECTED COUNT form) is the operator's and is not in this row. (plan rev 1, header and heading 1, ask638/w4/plan638a.md md5 7ff14cb7)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write it" at 08:23 CST 2026-11-25 on W4's card (Wall 12075; audit 42231), engine 393bca2e to ebf1dbcf, after W1's recheck PASS of the rebased target b2 1674abcb (Wall 12070), and read back PASS by W1 (Wall 12076: W1 built 638 A and then 645 on its own copy of 393bca2e and the result equals live 8470161f in all 426 nodes and the connections; standing 31 PASS 0 FAIL; t638 27 pass 1 fail, the one fail being C4 "only Shared Library changes", expected because ASK 645's QR nodes are in the same engine). Shared Library only, four LIB lines: 1366 (the cure result records the dropped premises), 1368 and 1501 (cpDrop returned, or null on the send-back path), 1556 (cureRewrite drops them before pkgCPD when the drop equals the cut, and writes the AUDIT v50 DERIVED line). Nothing was deleted. IN PART, because no run has been made since the write. History: plan rev 0 (d2c7954d) PASS WITH N1 (Wall 12051: the array is not inert; name its readers and report K-G8 and drv_uncured). Build b1 (target a6073640) was graded FAIL F1 by W1 (Wall 12059: the code is right, but "drv_uncured does not change" held for K-G8 only; the LIVE D38 BASIS check and the enforcer prompt line can change what a judge is sent, against the plan header). W4 answered with a gate replay and plan rev 1 (Wall 12061), and W1 graded build b1 with that answer and plan rev 1 PASS (Wall 12062). Offline: on sol's 42528 judgment the array goes from [3,4] to [3] with count 1; on sol's 42528 gate there are 0 D38 items old and new and the 13 gate items are equal, so sol's drv_uncured (9) is unchanged; a synthetic case raises one LIVE BASIS item, which if left uncured counts in drv_uncured. One deviation from the plan, a guard: the drop also requires that the array then has the count's length, and a count of 0 is left to pkgCPD. W4 corrected its own Wall 12057: D1 vs C3 was UNDERDETERMINED at the gate; CHALLENGER LINK BROKEN is its later stored grade. Scale by SQL (W4): 17 stored judgments carry both a CURED "takes the premise out of the count" line and a NOT DERIVED line. NOT CHECKED by W1: the late gate (row 54585); 42373; the audit rows. Open: two clean live runs; part B.$t$,
